From f5a7754d8d3f032635b0feaf6e1851b8e888354f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:12:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] ##arch: Emulate USSE register-file accesses and mov
 repeats

Give ESIL to two more groups whose semantics are pinned:
- ldr and str reach the SGX register file by a dword index, from an
  immediate or a register: register offset = index * 4. The hardware
  returns CORE_ID for "ldr rD, #7" and a page-directory base register for
  its index, and the firmware programs its registers this way, using the
  same index in a register for the same register. The registers are not
  in the USSE's 32-bit address space, so ESIL places them in a window at
  0x100000000 + offset; map memory there to emulate them. The window is
  plain memory: side effects of registers and the drc wait are not
  modelled.
- mov.repeatN between register ranges that do not overlap, unpredicated,
  as N moves with unit increments: the vertex and state-copy programs that
  ran on the hardware copy their attributes to the outputs this way. The
  MOE state that smlsi and friends set is not tracked.
ldr and str also set op->direction. The index registers, the 16-bit ALU
ops and the p sign test stay unmodelled. The SGX545 microkernel goes from
71.7% to 81.0% of its words with ESIL. Five new test/db/esil/usse tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
